WEBVTT

00:32:58.894 --> 00:33:01.708
that could at least get us
over to the other side,

00:33:01.732 --> 00:33:04.336
where we can have
a different conversation.

00:33:04.360 --> 00:33:07.401
Being around the country
talking to weavers, I've seen:

00:33:07.425 --> 00:33:09.450
A, this is a make-or-break moment on race.

00:33:09.474 --> 00:33:13.151
I really have come to think that with
the election of Trump and all the rest.

00:33:13.175 --> 00:33:18.818
B, there's just so much anger
in so many conversations I've had.

00:33:18.842 --> 00:33:21.212
Of course, we're all
aware of it intellectually,

00:33:21.236 --> 00:33:25.869
but when you spend your days having dinner
with folks in South Carolina or wherever,

00:33:25.893 --> 00:33:27.377
Chicago, New Orleans,

00:33:27.401 --> 00:33:32.724
and you see the level of
not just indignation but pessimism ...